        {"english": "Our Lord and Master", "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "GEIAD", "pronunciation": "ie in as ien tle iad-as iade, / Ge jad.", "printed": "........ (lost)"}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "Ge-iad"}}, "uncertain": true, "note": "Damaged in the print. The capitals line printed as dots; word from the pronunciation \"Ge jad.\" (j = I), with a pronunciation note above it ('ie in as ien tle, iad as iade'). Uncertain: no capitals survive, so spelling and word division rest on the pronunciation alone", "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 191, "leaf": 280, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 121, "leaf": 210, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 111, "leaf": 141, "field": "gd"}]},
