      "key": 18,
      "casaubonCall": 14,
      "dictated": "Saturday 14 May 1584, Cracow (\"Saturday, 14 Maii, Mane hora 6 Fere. + Cracoviae.\", p.118 n207); the English Thursday 5 July 1584 (p.189 n278, which names the 14 invocations \"received 14 Maii\").",
      "note": "Follows \"That is the thirteenth\" (p.137 n226); English margin \"18 / [14]\" (p.194 n283) and \"Δ This is the 14 as I received them in the holy Language.\" Casaubon's print of the 14 May calls (pp.133-138) is damaged and out of order: lacunae printed as dots, and fragments of Keys 12, 13, 16 and 17 interleaved on pp.135-137 (the manuscript, Cotton Appendix XLVI, was damaged). The Enochian of Keys 14 and 15 and of the first 14 words of Key 16 is not printed at all; only a few of their words survive in the English pages' margins and in Dee's list of first words, p.200 n289 (12 July 1584).",
      "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 88, "leaf": 181, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 193, "leaf": 282, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 194, "leaf": 283, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 79, "leaf": 172, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 80, "leaf": 173, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 137, "leaf": 226, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 138, "leaf": 227, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 123, "leaf": 153, "field": "gd"}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 124, "leaf": 154, "field": "gd"}],
      "checked": {"date": "2026-11-10", "works": ["casaubon1659", "equinox1912no8"], "covered": ["enochian", "english", "gd"], "notCovered": ["Sloane MS 3191, Dee's own copy, whose images are offline", "a second reading of every word (a random quarter was read twice)", "the words Casaubon's print has damaged"]},
      "rows": [
        {"english": "O thou", "englishSplit": true, "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "ILS", "pronunciation": "Ils.", "printed": "... (lacuna, three dots)"}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "ILASA"}}, "uncertain": true, "note": "Damaged in the print. The capitals column lost; pronunciation column prints \"Ils.\". Crowley prints ILASA, which looks like the GD sounding-out of ILS (cf. OL SONF VORSG -> \"Ol sonuf vaoresaji\"); Casaubon p.136 (n225) also prints ILS. as a word in another call. Dee reading ILS (uncertain: the lacuna has three dots, consistent with three letters); GD reading ILASA. Read a second time and confirmed on n226: capitals column \"...\", pronunciation \"Ils.\"; Dee's list p.200 n289 has \"19. O thou mighty light / Il micalZo al part\" (Il, not Ils), and Key 17 opens \"ILS.\" in the pronunciation column (p.136). ILS kept, uncertain; ILASA is the GD reading.", "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 193, "leaf": 282, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 137, "leaf": 226, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 123, "leaf": 153, "field": "gd"}]},
        {"english": "mighty", "englishSplit": true, "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "MICAOLZ", "pronunciation": "Mi ca ol zod.", "printed": "........ (lacuna)"}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "micalazoda"}}, "note": "Damaged in the print. The capitals column lost; word from the pronunciation column; Crowley agrees.", "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 193, "leaf": 282, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 137, "leaf": 226, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 123, "leaf": 153, "field": "gd"}]},
        {"english": "light,", "englishSplit": true, "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "OLPIRT", "pronunciation": "Ol pirt.", "printed": ".L.IRT (damaged)"}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "olapireta"}}, "note": "Damaged in the print. The capitals partly lost; pronunciation complete; Crowley agrees.", "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 193, "leaf": 282, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 137, "leaf": 226, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 123, "leaf": 153, "field": "gd"}]},
        {"english": "and burning flame", "englishSplit": true, "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "IALPRG", "pronunciation": "Yal. / I al purg."}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "ialpereji"}}, "note": "English line \"and burning flame of comfort\" split over IALPRG / BLIORS. No separate row for \"and\" (the app's earlier text (2023) has one). Casaubon p.193 (English), p.137 (Enochian).", "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 193, "leaf": 282, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 137, "leaf": 226, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 123, "leaf": 153, "field": "gd"}]},
