        {"english": "a window", "englishSplit": true, "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "COMO", "pronunciation": "Co mo bli ort.", "printed": "COMOB -- IORT (damaged, one line)"}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "como"}}, "note": "Damaged in the print. The capitals print \"COMOB -- IORT\" as one; pronunciation \"Co mo bli ort\" gives COMO + BLIORT; Crowley \"como belioreta\" agrees. English line \"a window of comfort\" split over COMO / BLIORT.", "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 194, "leaf": 283, "field": "english"}, {"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 138, "leaf": 227, "field": "enochian"}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 124, "leaf": 154, "field": "gd"}]},
