        {"english": "to the providence", "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "YARRY", "pronunciation": "Yár ry.", "printed": "[Y]ARRY"}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "yareryo"}}, "note": "capitals begin with a decorated woodcut initial Y followed by \"ARRY\". The archive.org scan of truefaithfulrela00deej is misbound: pp.203-204 sit at leaves n286-n287, and pp.197-198 appear again at n292-n293 where pp.203-204 belong", "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 203, "leaf": 286}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 125, "leaf": 155, "field": "gd"}]},
        {"english": "of him that sitteth on the holy Throne", "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "IDOIGO", "pronunciation": "Id ůi-go. / I d oi go.", "printed": "ID*UIGO *O"}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "IDOIGO"}}, "slot": "idoigo", "note": "The Golden Dawn varies this name with the Aethyr; Dee does not. The capitals printed \"ID*UIGO *O\": Dee's note says the wicked power so dazzled E.K. that he took this O for a V, and afterwards corrected it; pronunciation column \"Id ui-go.\" (a small circle over the u) then \"I d oi go.\"; Ilemese then: \"Where the most force was, the Devil crept most in\"; Dee: \"It must be then I doigo?\". Crowley p.125 n.2: \"This name may be appropriately varied with the Aire\" (he gives no replacement on pp.124-127)", "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 203, "leaf": 286}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 125, "leaf": 155, "field": "gd"}]},
        {"english": "and", "readings": {"casaubon1659": {"word": "OD", "pronunciation": "Od."}, "equinox1912no8": {"word": "od"}}, "sources": [{"work": "casaubon1659", "page": 203, "leaf": 286}, {"work": "equinox1912no8", "page": 125, "leaf": 155, "field": "gd"}]},
